# Confirmed findings

1. **Licence to wait — high**  
   **Offending text:** “If it will not go into those words, you have a feeling, not a finding — and the next four items wait until it does.”  
   **What is wrong:** This makes work-specific evidence an undated gate and explicitly suspends every subsequent action. Both reviewers found this independently.  
   **Evidence:** [CONTEXT.md §3](/home/diablo/book4/CONTEXT.md:265), rule 2: “Every evidence standard needs an expiry.”  
   **Fix:** “If it will not go into those words, you have a feeling, not a finding. Put the date in anyway, and use the four weeks before it to gather and give work-specific feedback.”

2. **Category overreach — medium**  
   **Offending text:** “By his own account, that is the cost side of three years of hiring…”  
   **What is wrong:** The 40% denominator is the team Groove launched with, not everyone hired during three years. The sentence silently broadens a cohort-specific turnover figure.  
   **Evidence:** [claims.tsv row 20/groove-fire-2015](/home/diablo/book4/checks/claims.tsv:550) says “turned over nearly 40% of the team we launched with”; the §6b Groove ledger preserves the same denominator.  
   **Fix:** “By his own account, that is the attrition Groove’s launch team suffered across its first three years…”

# Rejected findings

- **Trial-period backwards causation:** “Early on” proves that Turnbull once withheld feedback during an existing trial; it does not establish when the trial was introduced. The source also calls the non-negotiable trial something learned from three years of experience, so “built in response” is not demonstrably backwards.
- **Decision already made:** “Trying to force a fit” does not prove Turnbull had not reached a judgment; the same source says he would “wait too long.” Reviewer B turns an ambiguous psychological sequence into a contradiction the source does not establish.
- **Dutch cap quotation unregistered:** The complete quotation is exact in `.cache/bw7-2026.raw`, while [the registered row](/home/diablo/book4/checks/claims.tsv:559) covers the operative €102,000/twelve-month cap. Section 5b requires the legal claim to be registered, not every trailing word as a separate row.
- **Part-time parenthetical unregistered:** The complete sentence is present in the cached Groove source, and [claims.tsv](/home/diablo/book4/checks/claims.tsv:551) already registers that quotation by a substantial identifying fragment. This is not an unregistered figure or unsupported claim.

The chapter is not publishable as-is because Monday’s first action directly violates the book’s standing constraint and can halt the entire prescribed sequence indefinitely. The single most important change is to remove that gate: set the decision date immediately and gather work-specific evidence before it.
